  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nOvernight lows will be a tad warmer Sunday night, though still \nbelow average. Fog development will once again be possible across \nNE OK and NW AR. By Monday, high pressure will be sliding east, \nwith southerly low level flow returning to the forecast area. This\nwill promote a warming trend into mid week, with highs warming \ninto the mid 70s Tuesday and Wednesday. An upper level low will \nmove east across N TX Tuesday, potentially leading to a few \nisolated showers across SE OK, but any rainfall likely remains \nnegligible. Then, on Wednesday, a shortwave will drop southeast \nthrough the central Plains, perhaps leading to some low rain and \nstorm chances across far E OK and NW AR. From here, a pair of cold\nfronts are projected to sweep through the region with deep \ntroughing developing over the eastern US and ridging to our west. \nDry northwest flow aloft and post-frontal high pressure are likely\nto keep conditions dry and seasonably cool through the weekend.",
